WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Strength and stiffness. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Separate deformation from failure

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: Stiffness describes deformation under load; strength describes resistance to failure. They are different design questions.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: A flexible ruler and a brittle sample can differ in stiffness and failure behavior; do not infer one from the other.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Load-response graph

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Material category alone does not guarantee strength, durability or safety.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Separate deformation from failure
